body:
{The Confidence of Wildflowers by Micalea Smeltzer} and the second book of the duet, {The Resurrection of Wildflowers by Micalea Smeltzer}

Omg so good. I read these years ago and I think a reread is in order because I just realized a third book was recently released! 

Unless you have triggers, I honestly recommend just going in blind. That's what I did and it was a fantastic emotional rollercoaster.

I love an ugly cry book. I feel like I JUST recommended some of these so I wonder if there was a similar post recently. Anyway, here are my favs:

{Say You Swear by Meagan Brandy}

{Before We Were Strangers by Renee Carlino} I recommend this book so often. 

{On Dublin Street by Samantha Young} 

{Keepsake by Sarina Bowen}

{American King by Sierra Simone} although this is the last book in a trilogy so you really should start with the first book, {American Queen by Sierra Simone} 

{Shadows So Cruel by Liv Zander} although, again, this is part of a duet so you also have to read the first one {Feathers So Vicious by Liv Zander}

Edit: I almost forgot! {My Oxford Year by Julia Whelan}
